 "traditions": [],
 "notes": "Old trade/fleet models cut to private-owner types: dropped 1900D and Metro III (airliners), King Air E90/B100 kept only as versions, Conquest I, Cessna 402 and 414, Challenger 605, Global Express, Falcon 50, G450, G500 (older/duplicate SKUs; family represented). Old models now archetype versions: 172 Skyhawk, 182 Skylane, SR22, M20U Ovation Ultra, Super Cub, DHC-2 Beaver, Baron 58, King Air C90/200/300/350, PC-12, TBM 700/900/960, Citation Bravo/CJ4/Latitude/Longitude/Mustang, G-44 Widgeon, A5. Ikarus C42 not added (Wikipedia page 404, no other source). No traditions: aircraft have no artisan-tradition axis. Pitts Special and Rutan Long-EZ use designer names (Curtis Pitts, Burt Rutan) as mk; no register entries for them."
